ative of person Hos 4:6 ; 1Sam 1:11 (opposed to זָכַר ), Lam 5:20 ; Isa 49:14 (|| עָזַב ), Ps 10:12 ; Ps 13:2 ; Ps 42:10 . \\ \\ b. accusative of sins Amos 8:7 ; Ps 10:11 (accusative omitted), cry Ps 9:13 (opposed to זָכַר ), compare, of distress, Ps 44:25 . \\ \\ c. voice of foes Ps 74:23 . \\ \\ d. followed by infinitive Ps 77:10 . Niph`al Perfect 3 masculine singular נִשְׁכַּח Eccl 9:5 , etc.; Imperfect יִשָּׁכַח Ps 9:19 , 3 feminine singular תִּשָּׁכֵחַ Jer 20:11 , etc.; Participle feminine singular נִשְׁכָּחָה Isa 23:16 , נִשְׁכַּחַת v Isa 23:15 , plural נִשְׁכָּ חִים Job 28:4 — be forgotten: subject of thing Gen 41:30 ( E ), Deut 31:21 ; Jer 20:11 ; Jer 23:40 ; Jer 50:5 ; Isa 65:11 subject person Ps 9:19 ; Ps 31:13 ; Eccl 2:16 , Tyre Isa 23:15 ; Isa 23:16 (under figure of harlot), subject זִכְרָם Eccl 9:5 מִנִּי רָ֑גֶל ׳ הַנִּשׁ Job 28:4 . Pi`el Perfect 3 masculine singular ׳ וגו ׳ שִׁכַּח י Lam 2:6 ׳ י hath caused to forget (be forgotten) in Zion assembly and sabbath. Hiph`il Infinitive לְהַשְׁכִּיחַ Jer 23:27 to make my people forget my name (2 accusative). Hithpa`el Ipmf. 3 masculine plural יִשְׁתַּכְּחוּ Eccl 8:10 they were forgotten in the city.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8660')\">BDB8660</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H7911')\">H7911</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8659')\">BDB8659</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8661')\">BDB8661</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>שָׁכַח</bdbheb><sub>102</sub> <b>verb</b> <highlightword>forget</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; <wrongReferenceRemoved/> and (Pi`el) <checkingNeeded/><ref ref=\"Eccl 11:25\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(21,11,25)\">Eccl 11:25</ref> (twice in verse); Aramaic <bdbarc>שְׁכַךְ</bdbarc> <placeholder5527/> is <highlight>find</highlight>); — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b><sub>86</sub> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbhe